  "content": {
    "id": "p34-q76-node",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "76",
    "prompt": "The derivative of $y=\\sqrt{x}(ax+b)^n$ is\n$$y'=\\frac{(ax+b)^{n-1}}{2\\sqrt{x}}h(x)$$\nfor some function $h$. Find $h(x)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$h(x)=a(2n+1)x+b$.\n\nUse the product rule and factor out $\\dfrac{(ax+b)^{n-1}}{2\\sqrt{x}}$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y'&=\\frac{(ax+b)^n}{2\\sqrt{x}}+an\\sqrt{x}(ax+b)^{n-1}\\\\y'&=\\frac{(ax+b)^{n-1}}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\bigl[(ax+b)+2anx\\bigr]\\\\y'&=\\frac{(ax+b)^{n-1}}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\bigl[a(2n+1)x+b\\bigr]\\end{align*}$$\nHence $h(x)=a(2n+1)x+b$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 38
  },
